WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.080
- In the wake of a violent riot

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.340
that ended in actually
taking over the U.S. Capitol,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.640
leaving at least five dead,

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.980
including one Capitol police Officer,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.730
cries for removing the President

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.510
as expediently as possible are coming

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.850
from both sides of the aisle.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.460
But this isn't an episode
of "The West Wing".

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.650
This is actually real life.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.010
Can the 25th Amendment actually be invoked

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.010
to remove President Trump from Office?

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:29.253
Is that a legal possibility?
(dramatic music)

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.070
Hey, LegalEagles, it's time

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.110
to think like a constitutional scholar,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
because we are through
the looking glass, people.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.700
We are in uncharted territory,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.210
because people are furious
with President Trump,

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.480
not just for potentially
inciting the violent mob

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.260
that eventually took over the Capitol,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.880
but also with his lack of
a response after the fact,

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.890
his inability to calm the crowd

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:55.600
and basically seeming like he was AWOL.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.700
People are suggesting that the President

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.230
is now incapable of
discharging his duties.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.380
So, what do we do in that situation?

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.970
Well, a lot of people have
pointed to the 25th Amendment,

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:08.580
which was created to have a backup plan

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.970
in case the President was incapacitated

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.940
or otherwise incapable of
performing their duties.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.870
Now, the U.S. Constitution's original plan

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.310
for what happens in the event

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.000
of a presidential disability
or inability to work

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.080
was simply for the Vice
President to take over.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.870
But that was pretty vague.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.960
It seems simple enough, but
Article Two, Section One,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.910
Clause Six of the Constitution

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.940
doesn't exactly explain how to decide

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.010
when a President is considered disabled

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.270
or unable to perform the
duties of the Office.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.900
So in 1967, Congress
passed the 25th Amendment,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.970
which was intended to provide clarity

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.240
in these really dire situations.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.780
And if you've ever seen "The West Wing",

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:47.930
you've probably seen a couple

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:50.700
of these 25th Amendment
scenarios play out,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.500
but this is real life.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.810
And the real 25th Amendment
has several sections.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:58.260
The first is Section Three,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.923
which is a part of the 25th Amendment

00:01:59.923 --> 00:02:02.740
that has actually been
invoked several times.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.810
Section Three of the
25th Amendment provides

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.350
that the President has the authority

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.390
to declare him or herself unable

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:11.210
to discharge the powers of the Office.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.310
If the President makes this declaration,

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.600
it officially transfers
authority of the Office

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.700
to the Vice President,

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.130
who exercises it as Acting President

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:22.060
until the actual President
reclaims their authority

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.750
by declaring that the
disability has ended.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.520
So, why in the world
would a President ever

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.540
willingly give a power
to the Vice President?

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.420
Well, it's generally in
times of medical emergencies

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.640
or sometimes even a
routine medical procedures.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:38.860
So for example, this could apply

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.450
if the President was having surgery

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.790
and knew that he or she was
going to go under the knife

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.510
and was going to be
incapacitated for that time.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:47.840
The key aspect of Section Three

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.500
is that the President has
discretion over when it applies

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.860
and when it ends.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.200
And this has happened before,

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.950
Ronald Reagan sent a letter suggesting

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.330
that he was invoking Section Three

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.510
of the 25th Amendment when he
underwent surgery for a polyp,

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.700
George H.W. Bush was Acting President

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:05.970
for about eight hours while
President Reagan was in surgery.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.010
And after that, President
Reagan took back his power

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.000
as the actual President.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.920
Similarly, when George
W. Bush was President,

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.670
he formally invoked Section Three

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.700
of the 25th Amendment twice
when he was anesthetized

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.140
for routine medical procedures.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:21.270
Each time, the Vice
President, Dick Cheney,

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.730
took over on both occasions.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.230
And then, when the President felt better,

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.440
was declared fit for Office,
and retook their power

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.500
as the President of the United States.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.660
And believe it or not, took the power away

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.440
from Vice President, Dick Cheney.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.040
But while this is an
interesting history lesson,

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.170
this is obviously not the scenario

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.880
that people are talking
about in January, 2021.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.870
What people are talking
about in the context

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.430
of basically forcibly
removed the President

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.810
from power refers to Section
Four of the 25th Amendment.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.840
And Section Four of the 25th Amendment

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.730
is far more complicated and
contested than Section Three.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.190
Following the siege of the Capitol,

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:04.290
there've been lots of calls
for invoking the 25th Amendment

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.160
and removing President Trump from power

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.020
and installing Vice President
Pence as the Acting President.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.630
Nancy Pelosi, the Speaker of the House,

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.790
has called for Chuck Schumer,
the minority Senate leader,

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:17.070
though soon to be majority leader,

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.100
former Chief of Staff, John Kelly,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.040
has called for President Trump's removal

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.150
via the 25th Amendment,

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:25.410
and even Mick Mulvaney,
who just resigned his post

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.450
and was the former Director of OMB,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.580
former Director of the CFPB,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:32.040
and the former White House Chief of Staff,

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.410
has suggested that the 25th
Amendment should be in play.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:37.020
And all of them are referring

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.130
to Section Four of the 25th Amendment.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:44.300
So, there is a process for
removing a President from power

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.560
who is either unwilling or unable

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.710
to transfer power themselves.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.360
It's actually never happened.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.620
The Section Four of the 25th Amendment

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:58.290
has never been invoked, and
obviously it's highly political.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.610
Now, what most people think about

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:02.160
when they think of the 25th
Amendment is a President

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.890
who has suddenly taken ill,
maybe was in a car crash

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.280
and is put on a ventilator,

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.700
or has to go into emergency
surgery for, I don't know,

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.550
a heart condition or any
of the million things

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:17.260
that could actually befall
of an actual human President.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.320
And if they are in an emergency,

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.170
if they're under surgery,
under general anesthetic,

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.750
or in a coma, then the
25th Amendment could apply,

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.500
because the President
wouldn't have the ability

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.660
to make the determination for themselves

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.110
that they have to transfer of power.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.730
At the same time, the
authors of the Amendment

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.100
also does it cover scenarios
where the President thinks

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.900
that he or she is totally fine,

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.140
but that the Vice President

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.610
and a majority of the Cabinet think

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.070
that the President is not actually fine.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.170
Remember that America is
a country that was created

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.930
in part because the colonists didn't want

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.810
to be ruled by King George the Third,

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.990
who was said to be suffering from madness.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.860
So, if a President is unwilling

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.190
to declare him or herself incapacitated,

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.860
then the Cabinet and the
Vice President may act.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:05:59.870
In these circumstances,

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.407
the Section authorizes the Vice President

00:06:01.407 --> 00:06:03.510
and a majority of either the Cabinet

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:06.390
or any other body established
by law acting jointly

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:09.230
to declare the President to be disabled.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:10.540
And for all intents and purposes,

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.010
we're talking about the Vice President

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.340
and the members of the
President's Cabinet,

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.550
of which there are 15 members.

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:19.480
Specifically Section Four of
the 25th Amendment provides

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:21.147
that quote, "Whenever the Vice President

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:23.077
"and a majority of either
the principle Officers

00:06:23.077 --> 00:06:24.527
"of the executive departments

00:06:24.527 --> 00:06:26.237
"or of such other body as Congress,

00:06:26.237 --> 00:06:27.837
"may by law, provide, transmit

00:06:27.837 --> 00:06:29.517
"to the President pro
tempore of the Senate

00:06:29.517 --> 00:06:31.437
"and the Speaker of the
House of Representatives

00:06:31.437 --> 00:06:32.360
"their written declaration

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.877
"that the President is unable
to discharge the powers

00:06:34.877 --> 00:06:36.297
"and duties of his Office,

00:06:36.297 --> 00:06:38.557
"the Vice President shall
immediately assume the powers

00:06:38.557 --> 00:06:40.830
"and duties of the Office
as Acting President."

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.947
Now, the key phrase here is,

00:06:42.947 --> 00:06:46.137
"The President is unable to
discharge the powers and duties

00:06:46.137 --> 00:06:47.560
"of the Office."

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:50.360
At the moment, President
Trump is not in a coma,

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.890
he's not incapacitated,

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.520
as most people would
generally define that word.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:57.370
And this might be a
little bit controversial,

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:58.540
but I think most people would agree,

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.230
he's not suffering from
something like dementia.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.030
So, it could be an open question

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:07.080
as to whether the President's
indecision or inability

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.940
to attempt to prevent the mob
that took over the Capitol

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.210
or to effectively run the country

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:16.770
in the wake of this horrible tragedy,

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.500
whether that qualifies
as the sort of inability

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.820
to discharge the powers
and duties of the Office

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:24.330
that is contemplated
by the 25th Amendment.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.560
Now, practically speaking,

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.780
the 25th Amendment requires a majority

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:30.800
of the Cabinet Officers
agree with the Vice President

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.770
the President is unable
to fulfill their duties.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:36.140
There are 15 Cabinet positions,
as we've talked about.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.150
So, the Vice President
would need a concurrence

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.980
of at least eight of
the 15 Cabinet Members

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.870
to activate a declaration
of Presidential disability.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.570
Now, let's put aside
for the moment the fact

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.860
that the Trump Cabinet is currently full

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.900
of acting Cabinet Members

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.780
and has lost a lot of the
Senate confirmed Cabinet Members

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.830
that I think the 25th Amendment
originally contemplates,

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.160
but we'll get back to that.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.450
But again, talking about the practicality

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.760
of this for the moment, once
a majority of the Cabinet

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.920
and the Vice President
notify the President pro tem

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:05.830
and the Speaker,

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:09.030
the Vice President immediately
assumes the power and duties

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:11.940
of the Office of Acting President,

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:14.390
but the drafters of the 25th
Amendment were well aware

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.860
that this opened up the possibility

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.640
that the President was
being removed solely

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.510
for political reasons,

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.320
like the country was just tired of him,

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:23.670
or the Vice President was plotting a coup.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.050
So, the Amendment gives the
President a way to get back in

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.700
and reclaim their power
from the Vice President.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.990
The way that works is this,

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.610
and it's a little bit complicated,

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.840
once the Vice President invokes
the Presidential disability,

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.530
the Vice President
becomes Acting President,

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.980
but the President then,
the original President,

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:44.220
at the time of their choice,
can transmit a written message

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:46.590
to the President pro tem and the Speaker,

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:48.340
that no disability exists

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.320
and that the President
should then resume power

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.990
of the Presidency, but the thing is,

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.440
the President doesn't get
that power back immediately.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.270
Once the President has made a declaration

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.780
that they are objecting to the decision

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.690
of the Vice President and the Cabinet,

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:02.810
the Vice President and the Cabinet

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.650
then have four days to respond.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.470
So, this sets up a potential showdown,

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:09.480
because the Vice President and
the majority of the Cabinet

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.310
have four days to contest this finding,

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.840
this objection by the President

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.750
if they think the President
is still incapable

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.160
of serving, of discharging the duties.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.400
So, if in those four
days, the Vice President

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.820
and the Cabinet still
believed the President

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:25.710
is unable to discharge the
powers and duties of the Office,

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:28.400
then the decision goes to Congress.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.730
And at that point, if two thirds

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.850
of both Houses of Congress
believe that the President

00:09:33.850 --> 00:09:36.450
is unable to discharge
the duties of Office,

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.300
then the Vice President
continues as Acting President

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.510
until that disability is resolved

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.200
or until the end of the term.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.550
But if the two thirds
margin is not obtained

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:47.910
or if Congress is in session at the time,

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.300
but doesn't vote on the
question within 21 days

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.450
of receiving the declaration,

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:53.580
then the President has
to resume the powers

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.400
and duties of the Office.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.750
Similarly, if Congress is
not in session at the time

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.990
and assembles but doesn't
vote within 21 days,

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.300
then the President presumes the powers

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.160
and duties of the Office.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:03.810
Like I said, this is complicated,

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:06.520
but really practically speaking,
the way it works is this,

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:09.760
the Vice President declares
the President is disabled.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.670
So at that point, if the
majority of the Cabinet agrees,

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:16.790
the Vice President immediately
becomes Acting President.

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.890
At that point, the President can object.

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:21.300
And let's say that the
President objects immediately

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.430
at the same time that the
Vice President takes power,

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.430
then the Vice President and
the Cabinet have four days

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.200
to decide if they agree.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.490
And if the Vice President
and Cabinet still believe

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:31.770
that the President is disabled,

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.990
then the decision goes over to Congress,

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:37.750
who have to act within
a maximum of 21 days,

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:40.110
although they can obviously act sooner.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:42.960
Now, as I said, Section Four
has never been activated

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.320
since the Amendment was ratified in 1967,

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.900
but there were two events
during Reagan's presidency

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:50.580
where arguably it should
have been invoked.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.710
On March 30th, 1981, President Reagan

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:54.010
was shot and seriously wounded

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.060
while leaving a speaking
engagement in Washington.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:58.590
It was actually just down
the street from where I live.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.790
President Reagan had emergency surgery

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.570
and he was under anesthesia.

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:05.300
His aides debated whether or
not to invoke Section Four

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:06.390
of the 25th Amendment.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.780
They were all notified that
a full recovery was expected,

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:12.030
and decided that no
further action was needed.

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:13.510
But when President Reagan was shot,

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:16.520
Al Haig, the Secretary of
State made a huge mistake

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:19.050
and told the press that he was in control

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.953
while the President was in surgery.

00:11:20.953 --> 00:11:25.410
- As of now, I am in control
here in the White House,

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.963
pending return of the Vice President.

00:11:26.963 --> 00:11:29.340
And I'm in close touch with him.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.860
If something came up, I would
check with him, of course.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:35.080
- This was considered a
huge mistake in faux pas

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:38.170
and sort of demonstrated
constitutional ignorance

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.540
by a high ranking official,

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.590
because the Secretary of
State is not the person

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:45.830
who takes over when the
President is incapacitated.

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:48.490
And while many people
remember Al Haig's comments

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:51.440
and the constitutional crisis
that it almost created,

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.930
fewer people are aware that Section Four

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:55.820
of the 25th Amendment was also in play

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.350
during the waning days of
the Reagan's presidency,

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.650
because in the last
days of the presidency,

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:03.320
his mental status was
also questioned by staff

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:04.740
while he was in Office.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.060
In 1987, former Senator Howard Baker,

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.470
President Reagan's newly
appointed Chief of Staff,

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.480
reportedly received a
memorandum from an aid

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:16.190
that claimed that the President
was inattentive and inept.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:17.840
The memorandum went on to urge Baker

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.350
to consider the possibility

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:22.450
that Section Four of the 25th
Amendment might be applied.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.050
Baker concluded that the
President was attentive and alert.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:30.850
And on March 2nd, after a
meeting, he dismissed this report.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.620
Of course, we all know how this ended,

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.690
because five years after President Reagan

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.070
left the presidency,

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:38.300
he was diagnosed with Alzheimer's Disease

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:41.770
and rarely made public
appearances after that.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.180
But fast forward 35 years to today,

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:46.910
and as much as we know
about the 25th Amendment,

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.640
there's actually a lot
that we don't know as well.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:50.897
We don't know if the key phrase,

00:12:50.897 --> 00:12:53.220
"Unable to do discharge the
powers and duties of his Office"

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:56.240
applies in this particular
situation with President Trump.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.390
If that was disputed,

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.630
we don't know what the
Supreme Court would say.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.400
It's entirely possible that,

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.210
if someone does disputed this application,

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:07.070
the 25th Amendment, assuming
that they even had standing,

00:13:07.070 --> 00:13:09.750
I suppose it would be a
deposed President Trump

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:13.070
who would be making the
claim, if they had standing,

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:14.550
it's entirely possible
that the Supreme Court

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.000
would call this a political question

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:17.850
and refuse to adjudicate it.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:20.940
And the really big known
unknown is the fact

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:24.330
that President Trump's Cabinet
is full of acting secretaries

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:27.190
because he basically just
stopped sending Cabinet Members

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:28.690
to be confirmed by the Senate.

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.660
At the moment, we have
Acting Cabinet Members

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.210
in charge of the Department of Justice,

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.950
the Department of Defense
and of Homeland Security,

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:38.420
as well as the Department of
Transportation, Elaine Chao,

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.610
Mitch McConnell's wife, just resigned

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:44.330
from being the Head of the
Department of Transportation.

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:45.850
But as law professor Brian Kalt,

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:49.100
who is basically the foremost
expert in the 25th Amendment,

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:50.580
explains a lot of people assume

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:53.910
that Acting Secretaries can't
vote on the 25th Amendment,

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.610
but at most it's unclear.

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:58.210
There's potential scholarly consensus

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:02.110
that the Acting Secretaries
can vote based mainly

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.710
on a 1965 House Committee report.

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:05.870
But again, it's unclear.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:09.610
And at most, if the Acting
Cabinet Members cannot vote,

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:12.240
then that would lower the
number of Cabinet officials

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.260
that would need to be in the majority

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:16.250
to invoke the 25th Amendment.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.960
But we also don't know
if this is a complete

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.460
and total pipe dream.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.100
People on the left have been calling

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.850
for invoking the 25th Amendment

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:24.360
against President Trump, basically,

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.310
as long as the President
has been in the Office.

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.270
And reports say that Vice President Pence

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.650
has no interest in invoking
the 25th Amendment,

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:34.640
despite the fact that there are calls

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.240
for him to invoke it
from across the aisle.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:41.283
What we do know is that if the
25th Amendment was invoked,

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:44.830
President Trump would no longer
be President immediately.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.390
And he wouldn't be President
for at least four days.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:50.300
Then an additional potential up to 21 days

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:53.920
would also prevent him
from retaking the Office,

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.270
even if Congress refused to do anything.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.370
And at the time of this recording,

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:02.410
there's only two weeks left
in the President's term,

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.010
and invoking the 25th
Amendment could keep him

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:08.280
out of all Office until
the end of his term.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:09.840
And additionally, the 25th Amendment

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:12.920
is not mutually exclusive
to impeachment and removal,

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:15.210
as others have called for as well.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.820
You can do both.

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:17.960
And on the other hand,

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:20.920
there might be a good reason
to invoke the 25th Amendment,

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.260
because it works immediately,

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:25.060
in part because it might be necessary

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:27.920
to prevent a massive wave of pardons.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.290
Right now, Bloomberg reports

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:32.010
that President Trump is
considering a whole raft of people,

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:35.510
including himself, Mark
Meadows, Stephen Miller,

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:39.590
John McEntee, Dan Scavino,
Ivanka Trump, Jared Kushner,

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:42.400
Rudy Giuliani, Kimberly
Guilfoyle, Albert Pirro,

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:45.090
Lil Wayne and Kodak Black.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.680
I'm gonna go out on a limb and opine

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:48.980
that that would be a bad thing.

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:51.160
But perhaps we're being too precious

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:53.380
with the Office of the Presidency.

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:56.420
The President is not a
king ordained by God.

00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.870
Lots of democracies have
votes of no confidence

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:01.610
that allow the legislatures
to kick out the top executive,

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:03.260
effectively whenever they want.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.240
And there's lots of good reasons

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.870
why you might want to do that.

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:10.650
And four years for a
President to serve their term

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.300
is a long time.

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:15.840
It's a long, long time.

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:18.240
But I leave that to you, do
you agree with my analysis?

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.740
Leave your objections in the comments

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.190
and check out this playlist over here

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:22.720
with all of my other real law reviews,

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.060
which talk about the crazy
legal issues of the day,

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:26.700
'cause there are a lot of them.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:29.793
So, click on this playlist
and I'll see you in court.

